---
import { REPO_URL, SHIPPED } from "../config";
import Logo from "./Logo.astro";
---

<section
  id="cta"
  class="relative flex flex-col items-center gap-5 overflow-hidden border-t border-rule px-0 pt-26 pb-23 text-center"
>
  <div
    class="glow pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 -bottom-[260px] h-[540px]"
    style="background:radial-gradient(42% 58% at 50% 100%,rgb(242 137 92 / 26%),transparent 70%)"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>

  <Logo size={76} class="float relative shadow-[0_22px_44px_-18px_rgb(242_137_92/60%)]" />

  <h2
    class="relative m-0 max-w-[19ch] font-display text-[clamp(32px,5.4vw,50px)] leading-[1.06] font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-balance"
  >
    One process. One grant of trust. Read the source.
  </h2>

  <p class="relative m-0 max-w-[52ch] px-5 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.6] text-fg/56 text-pretty">
    A program that holds every credential you own should be readable and compilable by the people
    trusting it. The licence is not settled yet, and that is a gap rather than a position.
  </p>

  {/*
    There is no download button, and the flag is why. `SHIPPED` gates the one
    element that would name something you can get; everything else on this page
    is true whether or not there is a release, which is the rule config.ts
    states — a string outside a SHIPPED branch has to stand on its own.
  */}
  <div class="relative flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3 px-5 pt-1.5">
    <a
      href={REPO_URL}
      rel="noopener"
      class="plate rounded-md px-6 py-3.5 text-[15px] font-semibold text-accent-ink shadow-[0_14px_34px_-14px_rgb(242_137_92/75%)]"
    >
      Read the source ↗
    </a>
    <code
      class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/5 px-4.5 py-3.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-fg/72"
    >
      make app && make audit
    </code>
  </div>

  {
    !SHIPPED && (
      <p class="relative m-0 text-[12.5px] text-fg/38">
        No release yet — the app is code-signed for development only.
      </p>
    )
  }
</section>
